Problem: Group Anagrams (LC 49)

Pattern:
Hash Map + Sorting

Approach:

1. Create a hash map where the key is a sorted version of a word and the value is a group of anagrams.
2. Go through every word in the input.
3. Save the original word because the word will be sorted to create the key.
4. Sort the characters of the word. Anagrams will produce the same sorted key.
5. Use the sorted word as the key and add the original word to its group.
6. After processing all words, create an answer list.
7. Go through the hash map and add every group to the answer.
8. Return the answer.

Time Complexity: O(n × k log k)

Space Complexity: O(n × k)

Here, n is the number of words and k is the average length of a word.
